<Project>

  <!--
    MSBuild auto-imports `after.<solution>.sln.targets` from the solution
    directory into the generated solution metaproj.

    The .NET 8 SDK's _CheckForSolutionLevelRuntimeIdentifier target hard-errors
    (NETSDK1134) whenever a solution is built with a global RuntimeIdentifier
    (`dotnet build HoardPad.sln -r <rid>`). HoardPad's per-milestone verify gate
    requires exactly that invocation for both shipping RIDs (build-context.md:
    "every milestone `dotnet build -r win-x64` AND `-r linux-x64` clean").

    The RID is legitimately propagated to each project — class libraries ignore
    it for a (non-publish) build, and HoardPad.App (RuntimeIdentifiers =
    win-x64;linux-x64) honors it. Only the solution-level *guard* is the obstacle.
    Redefining that one target as a no-op lets the RID flow to the projects while
    keeping the documented gate command intact. The R2R publish guard in
    Directory.Build.targets is unaffected (it fires on Publish, per project).
  -->
  <Target Name="_CheckForSolutionLevelRuntimeIdentifier" />

</Project>
